# URL consistency

URLs are bookmarked, shared, and indexed — keep them readable and stable.

- **Never put a database id in a URL.** Use slugs (`slugify(city.name)`), not cuids — in paths and query params (`?city=bengaluru`, not `?city=cmrkwg8gk…`).
- **Prefer paths over query params** for rankable pages (e.g. `/bengaluru/buy/apartments` vs `/?city=…&category=…`). Query params filter an page that already has its own URL.
- **Query-param variants of a rankable page need a canonical** to the plain route (same pattern as homepage `alternates.canonical`).
- **When changing URL shape**, accept the old form as fallback or add a 301 — silent fallback to a default breaks shared links unnoticed.
- **Be consistent app-wide** — one divergent builder reintroduces id-based query params.
